# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Shuwei Li et al. (2026). Melt-Quench Failures and Practical Solutions for Universal Machine-Learning Interatomic Potentials in Amorphous Structure Generation.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2606.16385  arXiv:2606.16385v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2606.16385v2 (sha256 a5003891af090473...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 298 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/li2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: eight universal MLIPs (Table S1) and an IrO2 MTP used in
# melt-quench MD of amorphous IrO2, the UPET (PET-OAM-XL) energy, mean-force
# and pressure errors against AIMD configurations before and after
# pressure-targeted fine-tuning (Fig. 4). Densities and the 30-material
# density benchmark (Table S2) are properties, not error metrics.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
