###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The force metric is the MAE of the per-configuration mean atomic force magnitude (Eq. 2) and the stress metric the MAE of the virial pressure (Eq. 3); pressures in bar are converted to GPa. Whether the UPET-FT parity configurations are the test split is not stated, so the role is unset.
# - GRACE, MTP and NequIP parity plots (Figs. S3, S4) and the density results (Figs. 1, 5, 6; Table S2: NVT-quench density MAE 0.35 g/cm3 vs 2.46 g/cm3 for NPT-quench against AIMD) are not energy/force/stress errors. MatterSim-v1-5M is the registry model MatterSim-v1; the other universal models are paper-local runs.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/li2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

